+4.  **Apply 1D Cubic Kernel:** For each dimension, apply a cubic filter kernel $K(u)$ to the 4 sampled values. The general form of the cubic kernel depends on parameters $B$ and $C$ (see [Cubic Interpolation (Mitchell-Netravali)](2073-cubic-interpolation-mitchell-netravali.md)), which control smoothing or sharpening [S3, unofficial]. For a specific dimension with values $v_{-1}, v_0, v_1, v_2$ and offset $f$, the interpolated value $v'$ is:
     $$ v' = K(f) \cdot v_0 + K(1+f) \cdot v_{-1} + K(1-f) \cdot v_1 + K(2-f) \cdot v_2 $$
